The nettle backend of util/random.c seeds yarrow from getentropy(3), but nothing
declares it on Darwin:

    util/random.c:192:5: error: call to undeclared function 'getentropy'; ISO C99
    and later do not support implicit function declarations

config.h declares getentropy itself only under `#ifndef HAVE_ARC4RANDOM`, i.e. on
the platforms where unbound also has to supply an implementation from compat/.
Darwin has arc4random, so it gets no declaration from there, and unlike glibc it
does not declare getentropy in <unistd.h> either.  The combination only shows up
with --with-nettle, since an openssl or libbsd build takes the arc4random branch
of this file and never reaches the nettle one.

--- a/util/random.c
+++ b/util/random.c
@@ -70,6 +70,11 @@
 #include "pk11pub.h"
 #elif defined(HAVE_NETTLE)
 #include "yarrow.h"
+#ifdef __APPLE__
+/* Darwin declares getentropy(3), which seeds yarrow below, in <sys/random.h> rather than
+ * <unistd.h>; config.h declares it itself only on the platforms where unbound supplies it. */
+#include <sys/random.h>
+#endif
 #endif
 
 /** 
